# Object model `global` size budget (hard stop)

RRF/DSF discards oversized `key=global` responses (~**8 KiB** with DWC flags `d99vno`):

`Cannot store excessively long object model response … key global`

DWC always polls the **whole** `global` key; plugins cannot split it. Headroom comes only from smaller globals.

## Boot overlay order (mandatory)

1. `nxt-vars.g` — lean core defaults  
2. `nxt-custom-globals.g` — only when Custom (`nxt-custom.requested` / overlays); `if { !exists }` → null  
3. Optional MOS import (nested: no double custom-globals / mid user-vars) → tooltable (owns `mosTT→nxtTT`) → probe-wcs if `!nxtWPDeg` → align WCS/OT  
4. `nxt-user-vars.g` — operator `set` overlay (omit unset keys)
4b. `nxt-probe-virtual.g` — persisted G6511 virtual after user-vars
5. … board / tools / workplaces / boot / plugin-init once / single RGB `M950` … 
6. **`nxt-user-overrides.g` last** → then `nxtLoaded`

UI Save paths (Configuration, Calibration, Custom Apply) must use `persistNxtUserConfig` so sentinels stay aligned.

## Rules for every agent (mandatory)

1. **Do not** add `global nxtCustom*` to [`nxt-vars.g`](../../macros/system/nxt-vars.g). Declare in [`nxt-custom-globals.g`](../../macros/system/nxt-custom-globals.g) with `if { !exists }`. Gate **A-axis** keys on `0:/sys/nxt-custom-a.requested`.
2. **Do not** pre-fill `nxtProbeResults` in `nxt-boot.g`. Leave slots `null` until a cycle writes them.
3. **Do not** allocate `nxtTT` with a filled template — use `vector(limits.tools, null)`.
4. **Do not** persist `set global.<optional> = null` in generated `nxt-user-vars.g`. Omit unset keys; declares belong in boot, not Save.
5. **Do not** add many small related globals when one packed vector works (e.g. `nxtRGBCol`). Prefer scalars over `vector(limits.tools)` for single-slot caches (`nxtToolCacheIdx`/`Z`).
6. **Warn / avoid** loading both `mosTT` and `nxtTT`.
7. **Do not** gate `nxt-probe-wcs.g` on `nxtOvertravel` — use `!exists(global.nxtWPDeg)`.
8. **Before** claiming vars/boot/Custom/persistence work is done, run: `node dist/check-om-global-budget.mjs` — must exit 0. Read the printed **estimate** line (lean / Custom / siblingsIdle); do not treat a green exit as “unlimited headroom” if siblingsIdle is near 8 KiB — filled tools, VFD status, and leftover `mosTT` still tip over.
9. Read [docs/OM_GLOBAL_SIZE.md](../../docs/OM_GLOBAL_SIZE.md). The checker **estimates** boot JSON size and **bans** known cliffs (e.g. filled `nxtToolLife`); it cannot see live `nxt-user-vars` string bloat on a printer.

## Patterns

```gcode
; ❌ BAD — Custom declares in nxt-vars.g
global nxtCustomAHomeAt = null

; ✅ GOOD — nxt-custom-globals.g (and any re-entry assign)
if { !exists(global.nxtCustomAHomeAt) }
    global nxtCustomAHomeAt = null
else
    set global.nxtCustomAHomeAt = null

; ✅ GOOD — nxt-user-vars.g overlay only (overwrites defaults)
set global.nxtCustomAHomeAt = 1
```

New globals: follow [nxt-global-lifecycle.mdc](nxt-global-lifecycle.mdc) (declare-or-set default → user-vars `set` overlay).
